00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:44,547 --> 00:01:47,546
I just got this tea. Try it.

2
00:02:00,186 --> 00:02:04,130
I heard you've been butting heads
with those old fossils again.

3
00:02:04,131 --> 00:02:05,784
Not really.

4
00:02:05,785 --> 00:02:07,850
It's just normal talk.

5
00:02:07,851 --> 00:02:09,879
Enough. Don't give me that.

6
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:14,546
I'm telling you, you should go along with them.

7
00:02:14,547 --> 00:02:17,399
Shareholders' meeting soon.
The board'll be reshuffled.

8
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:23,359
At a time like this,
you know what matters most and what doesn't.

9
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,747
Dad.

10
00:02:25,592 --> 00:02:30,624
Since when did our family have to
sacrifice a woman's career dreams

11
00:02:30,625 --> 00:02:33,850
to shore up our footing
at the shareholders' meeting?

12
00:02:33,851 --> 00:02:34,875
No.

13
00:02:34,876 --> 00:02:37,458
Aren't you also going to marry her?

14
00:02:37,459 --> 00:02:39,684
If that's the case, get it done sooner.

15
00:02:39,685 --> 00:02:42,510
Once you're married, she can't fly, can she?

16
00:02:44,166 --> 00:02:47,679
But if she can't fly after marrying me,

17
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:51,097
what makes me think she'll definitely marry me?

18
00:02:52,594 --> 00:02:56,053
You should leave this matter to me.

19
00:03:00,693 --> 00:03:04,479
The tea's good. It's just a little hot.

20
00:03:05,259 --> 00:03:07,045
You drink it.

21
00:03:09,406 --> 00:03:11,787
You're still too young.

22
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:16,160
[Episode 21]
[Some Periods Precede a New Chapter]

23
00:03:37,324 --> 00:03:41,381
Hello, everyone. I'm Lu Zheng Yang, an
investigator with Hengshi's Safety Committee.

24
00:03:41,382 --> 00:03:44,333
Here are my credentials.
These three are on the investigation team.

25
00:03:44,334 --> 00:03:47,849
We called this emergency meeting today
to investigate Hengshi Air Flight 5123,

26
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:51,754
which failed to stop
within the landing distance.

27
00:03:51,755 --> 00:03:53,371
I'm Ruan Si Xian.

28
00:03:53,372 --> 00:03:56,344
Flight 5123 was flying to Jiang City.

29
00:03:56,345 --> 00:03:58,610
I was in the right seat.
I was the pilot monitoring.

30
00:03:58,611 --> 00:04:01,319
After the captain became incapacitated,
I declared an emergency.

31
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:04,024
Then I took over the controls
and became the pilot flying.

32
00:04:04,025 --> 00:04:06,679
At the time, the weather was extremely bad.

33
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,319
Strong winds and moderate rain showers.

34
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,320
So...

35
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,543
<i>What would it take to change your mind?</i>

36
00:04:14,544 --> 00:04:17,663
<i>When the sun rises from the west.</i>

37
00:04:18,596 --> 00:04:21,243
<i>No wonder you're the kind of woman
who can send people flying.</i>

38
00:04:21,244 --> 00:04:23,588
<i>I can send people to the grave.</i>

39
00:04:23,589 --> 00:04:25,372
<i>You don't want to be my boss,</i>

40
00:04:25,373 --> 00:04:27,342
<i>but want to be my boyfriend instead?</i>

41
00:04:28,137 --> 00:04:29,439
<i>In your dreams.</i>

42
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:34,434
<i>To judge how well a refrigerator works,
do I have to freeze inside it for two days?</i>

43
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:45,971
Mr. Fu.

44
00:04:47,366 --> 00:04:48,744
Mr. Fu.

45
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,271
They're all here.

46
00:05:50,351 --> 00:05:51,359
Hello.

47
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:52,479
Fu Ming Yu.

48
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:54,518
Can my mom meet Ruan tonight?

49
00:05:54,519 --> 00:05:57,729
Otherwise, she won't stop worrying.
We're almost there.

50
00:05:57,730 --> 00:05:59,150
Okay.

51
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,664
- Got it.
- Okay.

52
00:06:03,665 --> 00:06:05,782
Well? What did he say?

53
00:06:06,726 --> 00:06:07,878
Go to Hengshi Air.

54
00:06:07,879 --> 00:06:11,318
Well, I'll turn around and head back.
Handle things at the airport for now.

55
00:06:11,319 --> 00:06:13,219
Okay. You can count on me.

56
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,841
Turn around.

57
00:06:23,918 --> 00:06:25,733
Auntie Dong. Over here.

58
00:06:41,117 --> 00:06:42,826
Ming Yu.

59
00:06:42,827 --> 00:06:47,397
Didn't she make a successful emergency landing
and save everyone on board?

60
00:06:47,398 --> 00:06:50,161
Why does she have to face an investigation?

61
00:06:50,162 --> 00:06:53,595
She won't get into trouble, right?

62
00:06:54,644 --> 00:06:58,960
This is all standard procedure.
Don't worry, Auntie Dong.

63
00:07:02,311 --> 00:07:05,482
I rarely get to see her in uniform.

64
00:07:05,483 --> 00:07:07,639
She looks incredible.

65
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:09,383
Beautiful and commanding.

66
00:07:09,384 --> 00:07:14,569
It's hard to believe
someone so petite can fly such a huge plane

67
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:16,903
and carry passengers around the world.

68
00:07:16,904 --> 00:07:21,013
She can even step up
and save the day in a crisis.

69
00:07:22,193 --> 00:07:24,115
She's remarkable.

70
00:07:25,673 --> 00:07:27,719
You know what?

71
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:31,450
Her name was meant to be Ruan Guang Zhi.

72
00:07:32,617 --> 00:07:34,398
Isn't that strange?

73
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:40,326
I remember when I was pregnant,
she was kicking up a storm in my belly.

74
00:07:40,327 --> 00:07:44,479
The old folks with experience all said
that it had to be a boy.

75
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,959
So her father was in a rush to give her a name.

76
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:51,801
Guang Zhi, meaning a steady heart,
broad ambitions, and nothing to fear.

77
00:07:51,802 --> 00:07:54,306
So why did you end up
giving her the name she has now?

78
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:57,643
When I was carrying her,

79
00:07:57,644 --> 00:08:01,947
her father was sent to the frontier
to teach at a school.

80
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:06,047
It was a tiny, remote place.

81
00:08:06,048 --> 00:08:08,553
There was only one phone in the village.

82
00:08:08,554 --> 00:08:12,133
So her father
and I wrote letters to each other.

83
00:08:12,134 --> 00:08:13,598
So many years have passed.

84
00:08:13,599 --> 00:08:16,378
I can't remember what we wrote about anymore.

85
00:08:16,379 --> 00:08:21,866
I only remember that every letter was signed
with the characters for Si Xian.

86
00:08:23,306 --> 00:08:25,770
I thought those two characters were beautiful.

87
00:08:25,771 --> 00:08:29,835
When she was born, I gave her that name.

88
00:08:30,951 --> 00:08:32,462
It sounds lovely.

89
00:08:33,675 --> 00:08:36,039
So, what happened after that?

90
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,147
After that,

91
00:08:38,148 --> 00:08:43,771
I got divorced from her father,
so I could study painting abroad.

92
00:08:43,772 --> 00:08:46,019
She never would accept me.

93
00:08:46,942 --> 00:08:50,971
She wouldn't take the child support I sent her.

94
00:08:50,972 --> 00:08:55,321
She's stubborn. I guess she takes after me.

95
00:08:55,322 --> 00:08:57,781
Then her father died.

96
00:08:57,782 --> 00:09:02,417
She was left on her own,
studying and working at the same time.

97
00:09:02,418 --> 00:09:04,871
She was so young.

98
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:10,942
Yet she grew up stumbling along.

99
00:09:12,013 --> 00:09:16,572
I know she must have suffered a lot.

100
00:09:17,745 --> 00:09:23,237
So, Ming Yu, please be good to her from now on.

101
00:09:25,513 --> 00:09:27,706
She really hasn't had it easy.

102
00:09:31,842 --> 00:09:33,589
Don't worry.

103
00:09:37,169 --> 00:09:42,504
If anything had happened to her today,
I would never forgive myself.

104
00:09:46,778 --> 00:09:49,897
Okay. Let's not talk about it.

105
00:09:49,898 --> 00:09:51,603
I'll head back first.

106
00:09:51,604 --> 00:09:53,425
Auntie Dong.

107
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,981
Aren't you waiting for Ruan?

108
00:09:56,984 --> 00:09:58,639
No need.

109
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:03,485
I saw her sitting there,
and that was enough for me.

110
00:10:03,486 --> 00:10:05,965
Besides, she must be exhausted today.

111
00:10:05,966 --> 00:10:08,801
Have her go back and get some rest.

112
00:10:09,669 --> 00:10:11,001
Okay.

113
00:10:33,668 --> 00:10:36,719
It's done, right?
Thanks for your hard work, everyone. Thank you.

114
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,519
Ruan.

115
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:40,439
How are you? You're holding up okay?

116
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,799
It's fine.

117
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,519
How's Captain Yue doing?

118
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:46,919
He's fine. He's always had vasovagal syncope.

119
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,718
The flight doctor has records of it.

120
00:10:48,719 --> 00:10:51,463
This time, it was probably triggered
by a sudden nosebleed.

121
00:10:51,464 --> 00:10:54,765
Vasovagal syn...?

122
00:10:56,107 --> 00:10:59,611
Vasovagal syncope.

123
00:10:59,612 --> 00:11:01,732
You can think of it as
fainting at the sight of blood.

124
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:05,945
Then can he keep flying in the future?

125
00:11:05,946 --> 00:11:07,409
Once he recovers, he'll be fine.

126
00:11:07,410 --> 00:11:09,835
But from now on,
he'll be under closer medical watch.

127
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:13,530
All right.
Stop worrying so much. Get some rest.

128
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:17,391
Thanks for your hard work, everyone.
I'll walk you out.

129
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:14,248
Ruan.

130
00:12:26,488 --> 00:12:28,691
Come on, stop crying.

131
00:12:30,547 --> 00:12:33,404
I understand why Xiao Zhen cries,
but why are you crying too?

132
00:12:33,405 --> 00:12:35,036
I'm not crying.

133
00:12:35,037 --> 00:12:38,061
I'm just... I'm happy.

134
00:12:38,062 --> 00:12:41,925
Otherwise,
I'd think my bar lost a free pair of hands.

135
00:12:41,926 --> 00:12:44,889
Now that you're here, I'm really happy.

136
00:12:44,890 --> 00:12:46,971
All right. Go back and rest.

137
00:12:46,972 --> 00:12:49,989
You've had a long day.
Get some real rest at home.

138
00:12:49,990 --> 00:12:51,594
Hurry back.

139
00:12:56,679 --> 00:12:58,599
- Mr. Fu.
- Mr. Fu.

140
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,192
Go back.

141
00:13:02,330 --> 00:13:04,906
- Bye, brother-in-law!
- Bye, brother-in-law!

142
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,394
Should I call him brother-in-law?

143
00:13:14,395 --> 00:13:16,599
I should call him my sister's husband.

144
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,639
The boss already said so.
He told us to call him brother-in-law.

145
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,452
Fine, then "brother-in-law" it is.

146
00:13:22,453 --> 00:13:24,589
- Let's head back and rest.
- Let's go.

147
00:13:27,706 --> 00:13:31,234
Stop laughing, Ruan Guang Zhi.

148
00:13:33,635 --> 00:13:36,359
Seriously? She told you that too.

149
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,014
That's a nice name.

150
00:13:38,015 --> 00:13:39,563
And it has meaning.

151
00:13:39,564 --> 00:13:41,403
I'll call you Guang Zhi from now on.

152
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,619
I tried to hide this name,
but I guess that's not working.

153
00:13:46,571 --> 00:13:49,799
Well, I really didn't think she'd come.

154
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:53,039
At parent-teacher conferences
or graduation ceremonies,

155
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:58,696
even though I knew she wouldn't come,
I still hoped she might surprise me.

156
00:13:58,697 --> 00:14:00,760
But every time, I was disappointed.

157
00:14:00,761 --> 00:14:03,516
So I stopped expecting anything.

158
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:13,802
Captain Ruan, in those last few minutes,
what were you thinking?

159
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:18,670
How to land the plane safely.

160
00:14:24,237 --> 00:14:30,162
But once I'd landed,
the first person I thought of was you.

161
00:14:33,011 --> 00:14:34,844
I'm flattered.

162
00:14:36,079 --> 00:14:39,199
I wondered if you were still mad.

163
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:44,513
I held a plane for you
and saved you from a major loss.

164
00:14:44,514 --> 00:14:47,856
I don't know if this'll win you back.

165
00:14:56,262 --> 00:14:57,399
What?

166
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,771
I'm apologizing.

167
00:14:59,846 --> 00:15:01,704
You're pretty self-aware.

168
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:04,625
I won't ever do it again.

169
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,464
Won't do what?

170
00:15:06,465 --> 00:15:09,001
I won't storm out of the house again.

171
00:15:09,002 --> 00:15:12,546
I won't let our problems
follow you onto the plane.

172
00:15:12,547 --> 00:15:17,399
I won't let you board that plane
with any regrets or sadness.

173
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:20,625
What if we're still
in the middle of a fight before I board?

174
00:15:20,626 --> 00:15:22,559
I'll surrender unconditionally.

175
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,981
No way. That's not fair.

176
00:15:25,964 --> 00:15:28,189
Whatever the case,
I'll take full responsibility.

177
00:15:28,190 --> 00:15:32,742
You just need to bring me back souvenirs
from every city you pass through.

178
00:15:32,743 --> 00:15:34,952
Anyway, not like today.

179
00:15:34,953 --> 00:15:36,217
You got it wrong.

180
00:15:36,218 --> 00:15:40,375
The mighty Captain Ruan won't be at fault.

181
00:15:40,376 --> 00:15:42,360
You'd better watch it.

182
00:15:42,361 --> 00:15:44,719
Haven't you checked your phone?

183
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:47,305
I'm a big deal now.

184
00:15:47,306 --> 00:15:48,759
Let's break up.

185
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,937
I'm going to find my guy.

186
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,380
Your guy?

187
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:56,104
Your guy is me.

188
00:15:56,105 --> 00:15:57,690
No, you aren't.

189
00:15:57,691 --> 00:16:00,110
You are what they call a "brother-in-law."

190
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:05,583
What? Tired from driving?

191
00:16:06,354 --> 00:16:10,496
I've got endless stamina.
I can go on even after getting home.

192
00:16:12,274 --> 00:16:14,393
What are you talking about?

193
00:17:07,843 --> 00:17:11,219
<i>Visual reference in sight.
Autopilot disengaged.</i>

194
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,290
<i>Spoilers. Reverse green. Brakes!</i>

195
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,719
<i>If not me, then who?</i>

196
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,239
<i>I'm the captain in command.</i>

197
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:29,439
<i>The day you're sitting in that seat,
you'll do the same.</i>

198
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:34,464
<i>As pilots, we put our passengers' lives
and safety above everything else.</i>

199
00:17:34,465 --> 00:17:39,219
<i>I'd do it again without hesitation.
And I don't regret it.</i>

200
00:18:19,713 --> 00:18:21,675
Sorry for waking you.

201
00:18:23,316 --> 00:18:24,794
I wasn't sleeping deeply.

202
00:18:25,553 --> 00:18:27,690
I need to go to the office today.

203
00:18:30,398 --> 00:18:32,547
Will I be grounded?

204
00:18:36,222 --> 00:18:39,853
Don't worry about that yet.
Get some rest today.

205
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,400
Don't hide it from me this time.

206
00:18:44,273 --> 00:18:49,208
Whether I'm grounded, tell me right away.

207
00:19:04,199 --> 00:19:09,707
No matter what happens, remember that I'm here.

208
00:19:24,999 --> 00:19:27,988
Go on. Get some sleep.

209
00:19:47,818 --> 00:19:49,439
What a joke!

210
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:55,079
Since when do online commenters
set our flight safety standards?

211
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:58,039
You should be grateful
that this didn't turn into a disaster.

212
00:19:58,040 --> 00:20:01,383
Should anything happen,
the public would tear us apart.

213
00:20:01,384 --> 00:20:05,298
Our office would've been drowned in backlash.

214
00:20:05,299 --> 00:20:08,323
This isn't about doubting
this female pilot's flying skills.

215
00:20:08,324 --> 00:20:12,399
It's about the fact that, in that situation,
she could've woken the unconscious captain.

216
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:15,065
That would've been a safer bet
for a smooth landing.

217
00:20:15,066 --> 00:20:18,595
He just faints at the sight of blood.
It wasn't a big deal.

218
00:20:18,596 --> 00:20:21,559
Then why did she insist on
handling the landing herself?

219
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:24,119
Was she just overconfident?

220
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:29,025
Or was this female pilot
trying to clear her own name?

221
00:20:29,026 --> 00:20:33,115
I heard that recently,
she failed the left-seat check.

222
00:20:33,116 --> 00:20:35,799
The examiner was Captain Yue Yang.

223
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:40,842
If you put it that way,
then where does that leave passenger safety?

224
00:20:41,569 --> 00:20:43,125
Is that all?

225
00:20:44,007 --> 00:20:46,728
I have one question for all of you.

226
00:20:46,729 --> 00:20:49,051
Did any of you look at the flight data?

227
00:20:52,605 --> 00:20:56,799
Since when do we judge flight standards
without data,

228
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,919
but by your assumptions?

229
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:04,305
As for what was going through her mind,
we judge a person by their deeds, not motives.

230
00:21:04,306 --> 00:21:06,530
We care about the final result.

231
00:21:06,531 --> 00:21:08,279
And the result is that

232
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:13,329
this pilot landed safely
in such severe weather conditions.

233
00:21:13,330 --> 00:21:17,264
She kept everyone on board safe and sound.
There was nothing wrong with that.

234
00:21:17,265 --> 00:21:20,519
"We judge a person by their deeds,
not motives."

235
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:22,575
Well said.

236
00:21:22,576 --> 00:21:25,719
You went so hard to defend this female pilot.

237
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:30,685
Is it because
of your special relationship with her?

238
00:21:34,558 --> 00:21:38,490
Our relationship has nothing to do
with this incident.

239
00:21:39,457 --> 00:21:46,343
Since you two are in an intimate relationship,
then you're biased in this matter.

240
00:21:46,344 --> 00:21:48,679
So I think you should step aside.

241
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:54,385
Does being my girlfriend mean
she deserves unfair treatment from you?

242
00:21:54,386 --> 00:21:57,399
This is easy to handle. Ground her.

243
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,959
It's not a permanent suspension.

244
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:02,759
Once this storm blows over,
she can retrain and take the evaluation again.

245
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:08,359
But today, this grounding notice
has to be issued by you, Mr. Fu.

246
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:13,259
This can prove
that you're not biased in this matter.

247
00:22:33,667 --> 00:22:39,060
I can state very clearly that
I won't issue the grounding notice.

248
00:22:39,061 --> 00:22:43,583
First,
issuing a grounding notice would be unfair.

249
00:22:43,584 --> 00:22:49,960
Second,
not issuing one is what the public wants.

250
00:23:06,275 --> 00:23:09,178
"Anyone who said women can't drive,
please stand up."

251
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:11,997
"Let's see
how hard that slapped you in the face."

252
00:23:12,840 --> 00:23:14,599
"I thought this had to be a man."

253
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,905
"Turns out it was a woman."

254
00:23:18,434 --> 00:23:21,379
"How do I win you over?"

255
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:24,407
"I thought you were gorgeous
the last time I saw you."

256
00:23:24,408 --> 00:23:26,442
"I didn't expect you to be this good."

257
00:23:27,224 --> 00:23:29,065
"I read the report."

258
00:23:29,066 --> 00:23:32,009
"You made an emergency landing
in strong crosswinds and torrential rain."

259
00:23:32,010 --> 00:23:35,719
"The runway was wet, and the plane skidded,
but you stopped it just in time."

260
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:38,544
"That's insane."

261
00:23:38,545 --> 00:23:41,239
I'm done reading.
There are too many good comments.

262
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:42,479
How about you, Captain Ruan?

263
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:45,858
How do you feel
with all this praise flooding in?

264
00:23:45,859 --> 00:23:49,242
I feel nothing.

265
00:23:49,243 --> 00:23:52,794
Because that's just what I should do.

266
00:23:52,795 --> 00:23:56,938
I don't care about that.
All I know is "Captain Ruan" is trending again.

267
00:23:56,939 --> 00:23:59,443
You should say something.

268
00:23:59,444 --> 00:24:02,228
To be precise, I'm making a comeback.

269
00:24:02,229 --> 00:24:04,399
Because I was famous before.

270
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:06,519
As for what I can say about this...

271
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:11,944
Well, tonight's drinks are on Captain Ruan.

272
00:24:11,945 --> 00:24:14,945
So the internet was right after all.
The richer people get, the stingier they are.

273
00:24:14,945 --> 00:24:17,239
We're only drinking these few glasses.

274
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:18,799
What's wrong with a few drinks?

275
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:21,274
Drink up. Have as much as you want.

276
00:24:23,553 --> 00:24:26,671
Why do I feel like you're not that happy?

277
00:24:28,254 --> 00:24:33,588
Because I don't know
if this is a blessing or a curse yet.

278
00:24:33,589 --> 00:24:36,241
Did you forget what happened to my mentor?

279
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:40,439
After what you pulled off,
why is the Safety Committee investigating?

280
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:43,624
I have no idea. Now I just wait for the result.

281
00:24:43,625 --> 00:24:45,491
It should be soon.

282
00:24:46,331 --> 00:24:49,835
We aren't celebrating
your company's review or rating.

283
00:24:49,836 --> 00:24:52,159
And it doesn't matter whether you're a hero.

284
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:54,010
So what are we celebrating today?

285
00:24:54,011 --> 00:24:56,519
That we're lucky. That we survived another day.

286
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:59,984
That's surviving a close call.
Ladies, isn't that something to celebrate?

287
00:24:59,985 --> 00:25:02,090
- Exactly.
- Cheers.

288
00:25:02,091 --> 00:25:03,719
Cheers.

289
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:05,119
Well said.

290
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:07,812
Tong Le, music. Let's get this party started.

291
00:25:07,813 --> 00:25:09,078
Come on.

292
00:25:11,241 --> 00:25:13,064
Come on.

293
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:33,323
Let's jump in. Let's get started.

294
00:26:44,252 --> 00:26:46,556
So where should we start?

295
00:26:46,557 --> 00:26:48,261
We need to improve efficiency.

296
00:26:48,262 --> 00:26:50,286
The QAR reform is urgent.

297
00:26:50,287 --> 00:26:51,990
What do we need?

298
00:26:51,991 --> 00:26:56,969
We need them to feel and believe
that we can make a difference.

299
00:26:56,970 --> 00:27:00,759
Think about it.
We need pilots, and pilots are human beings.

300
00:27:00,760 --> 00:27:05,343
<i>I heard the board is forcing Mr. Fu
to issue your grounding notice.</i>

301
00:27:05,344 --> 00:27:08,182
<i>Mr. Fu has been holding the line.</i>

302
00:27:08,183 --> 00:27:11,663
<i>It's also tied to the shareholders' interests.</i>

303
00:27:11,664 --> 00:27:15,950
<i>He's been under great pressure lately.</i>

304
00:27:16,976 --> 00:27:19,505
Okay. Got it.

305
00:27:35,685 --> 00:27:37,302
<i>You have to trust him.</i>

306
00:27:37,303 --> 00:27:39,279
<i>I'm a good example.</i>

307
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:41,183
<i>Being grounded may not be a bad thing.</i>

308
00:27:41,184 --> 00:27:43,769
<i>The sooner you're grounded,
the sooner you might be back in the air.</i>

309
00:27:43,769 --> 00:27:45,919
<i>Don't wear yourself out over it.</i>

310
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:50,437
<i>If you've got nothing going on,
come by the house and help me watch the kid.</i>

311
00:27:51,688 --> 00:27:53,437
Yes.

312
00:27:55,650 --> 00:27:58,954
<i>The board is just making a big deal out
of your relationship.</i>

313
00:27:58,955 --> 00:28:02,820
<i>But don't worry. Mr. Fu will handle it.</i>

314
00:28:02,821 --> 00:28:04,879
<i>That's all for now. Don't worry.</i>

315
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:07,266
Okay. Got it.

316
00:28:20,346 --> 00:28:23,039
<i>I'm a little busy today. I'm not done yet.</i>

317
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:25,519
<i>Don't wait up for me. Get some rest.</i>

318
00:28:28,276 --> 00:28:34,128
[Are things not going well?]

319
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:45,275
<i>Okay. You get some rest too.</i>

320
00:29:20,167 --> 00:29:24,307
<i>Just meeting someone like you
is more than enough for me.</i>

321
00:29:25,068 --> 00:29:26,652
<i>But...</i>

322
00:29:26,653 --> 00:29:32,975
<i>if we weren't together,
wouldn't you have to struggle like this?</i>

323
00:29:38,966 --> 00:29:42,467
You look at me every day.
Aren't you tired of it yet?

324
00:29:44,458 --> 00:29:45,948
I can't get enough.

325
00:29:46,811 --> 00:29:48,755
I could never get enough of you.

326
00:29:56,669 --> 00:29:58,765
When did you get back?

327
00:30:03,638 --> 00:30:08,011
If I remember right, it was around 4 a.m.

328
00:30:08,012 --> 00:30:09,552
Something like that.

329
00:30:09,553 --> 00:30:13,249
Did everything go smoothly?

330
00:30:16,484 --> 00:30:18,117
You promised me.

331
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:24,526
No matter how it turned out,
you'd tell me the truth.

332
00:30:31,667 --> 00:30:35,141
It didn't exactly go smoothly, but it's okay.

333
00:30:35,980 --> 00:30:40,882
Give me a little more time. I can handle this.

334
00:30:40,883 --> 00:30:42,162
Trust me.

335
00:30:49,465 --> 00:30:51,767
Do you have any plans today?

336
00:30:56,695 --> 00:30:58,531
Today,

337
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,161
I want to go on a date with you.

338
00:31:05,979 --> 00:31:07,849
A date?

339
00:31:07,850 --> 00:31:10,135
Like a real couple.

340
00:31:11,138 --> 00:31:16,546
We've been too busy before
and never had time for a proper date.

341
00:31:20,291 --> 00:31:22,904
Then no work today.

342
00:31:22,905 --> 00:31:24,780
Let's go on a date.

343
00:31:25,633 --> 00:31:27,209
Where do you want to go?

344
00:31:29,983 --> 00:31:31,609
The amusement park.

345
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:51,674
Slow down. Watch your step!

346
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:03,519
This isn't exciting enough.

347
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:05,119
Let's go ride the roller coaster.

348
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:06,854
The roller coaster?

349
00:32:20,752 --> 00:32:22,496
Are you okay?

350
00:32:22,497 --> 00:32:24,077
Not really.

351
00:33:24,702 --> 00:33:26,915
The sunset today is beautiful.

352
00:33:30,606 --> 00:33:31,719
Hi there!

353
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:33,880
Do you want to take a picture?
You'll get it right away.

354
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:35,759
The lighting is perfect right now.

355
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:38,558
Are you dating? You'll look great in photos.

356
00:33:38,559 --> 00:33:40,559
- Well...
- Let's take one.

357
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:42,279
Take one.

358
00:33:42,280 --> 00:33:43,479
- Okay.
- Okay!

359
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:45,639
This way.

360
00:33:45,640 --> 00:33:48,537
Come here. Get a little closer.

361
00:33:48,538 --> 00:33:51,879
Three. Two. One.

362
00:33:55,051 --> 00:33:56,897
- Here you are.
- There, that's the shot.

363
00:33:56,898 --> 00:33:58,240
- Do you want another one?
- That's good.

364
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:00,599
- Okay. One more.
- Okay. Change your pose.

365
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:03,677
Three. Two. One.

366
00:34:08,130 --> 00:34:11,570
- You look amazing. Okay, thanks.
- Let me pay.

367
00:34:12,514 --> 00:34:13,578
Sure.

368
00:34:13,579 --> 00:34:14,764
Thanks.

369
00:34:14,765 --> 00:34:15,839
- There it is.
- Wow.

370
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:17,385
- Looks good.
- Not bad at all.

371
00:34:18,673 --> 00:34:21,979
I don't have anywhere to put it. You keep it.

372
00:34:28,617 --> 00:34:31,133
The sunset is beautiful.

373
00:34:32,575 --> 00:34:35,958
I haven't seen a sunset this beautiful
in a long time.

374
00:34:35,959 --> 00:34:38,960
I always feel like I'm rushed every day.

375
00:34:38,961 --> 00:34:42,145
Though I can still see the sunset while flying,

376
00:34:42,146 --> 00:34:47,716
without the sea breeze and waves,
it just feels ordinary.

377
00:34:47,717 --> 00:34:50,359
Maybe someday, when I can't fly anymore,

378
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:55,465
I'll miss those days
when I watched the sunset from the cockpit.

379
00:35:03,041 --> 00:35:06,233
Why are you suddenly saying this?

380
00:35:07,643 --> 00:35:09,506
I'm talking about retirement.

381
00:35:09,507 --> 00:35:14,174
Or do you want me to work for you
for the rest of my life?

382
00:35:21,281 --> 00:35:22,905
What's with the nerves?

383
00:35:22,906 --> 00:35:24,193
No.

384
00:35:25,112 --> 00:35:26,889
I'm not nervous.

385
00:35:26,890 --> 00:35:28,798
I'm very laid back.

386
00:35:29,538 --> 00:35:31,098
Very relaxed.

387
00:35:32,235 --> 00:35:36,216
Good. You're as laid-back as they come.

388
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:02,001
Fu Ming Yu.

389
00:36:04,761 --> 00:36:06,974
After the sun goes down...

390
00:36:12,140 --> 00:36:14,626
The sun hasn't set yet.

391
00:36:35,361 --> 00:36:37,914
The sun has set.

392
00:36:37,915 --> 00:36:42,021
- We--
- I know what you want to say. I don't agree.

393
00:36:45,687 --> 00:36:50,719
I've told you that I can handle this.

394
00:36:50,720 --> 00:36:53,230
I need you to trust me on everything.

395
00:36:54,595 --> 00:36:56,506
I'm the one who's tired.

396
00:36:57,680 --> 00:37:00,528
Do you know how hard my early life was?
How much I struggled to get by?

397
00:37:00,529 --> 00:37:04,879
Do you know how hard I've worked for this?
I gave it everything I had.

398
00:37:07,266 --> 00:37:11,702
Maybe heaven is telling us

399
00:37:12,763 --> 00:37:15,043
that we just don't fit.

400
00:37:16,861 --> 00:37:19,675
Actually, I think breaking up is better.

401
00:37:19,676 --> 00:37:22,089
You don't have to be so torn up.

402
00:37:22,090 --> 00:37:24,760
And I don't have to be, either. Really.

403
00:37:24,761 --> 00:37:27,866
Whether we fit or not should be up to us.

404
00:37:27,867 --> 00:37:29,467
Ruan Si Xian.

405
00:37:29,468 --> 00:37:33,353
You don't need to care about anyone
or anything besides our relationship.

406
00:37:33,354 --> 00:37:35,219
Why are you still not getting it?

407
00:37:35,220 --> 00:37:40,227
If we're not together,
these problems of ours wouldn't even exist.

408
00:37:40,228 --> 00:37:43,021
I love my flying career.

409
00:37:43,022 --> 00:37:46,705
Compared with our relationship,
I love my flying career more.

410
00:37:46,706 --> 00:37:50,783
I want to start over.
I don't want this to end like this.

411
00:37:53,074 --> 00:37:57,081
Actually,
this is a pretty good way to part in peace.

412
00:37:57,082 --> 00:37:58,424
Look.

413
00:37:59,453 --> 00:38:01,919
Look how beautiful the sunset is.

414
00:38:01,920 --> 00:38:07,896
It's like it's bringing our story
to a perfect close.

415
00:38:15,192 --> 00:38:18,210
Issue the ground notice early.

416
00:38:18,211 --> 00:38:22,894
The earlier you issue it,
the earlier I can get back in the air.

417
00:38:25,195 --> 00:38:29,180
Didn't you promise me
that you'd never just throw me away?

418
00:38:29,181 --> 00:38:31,483
Don't be childish.

419
00:38:33,023 --> 00:38:40,241
I toss aside anyone or anything
that keeps me from flying like trash.

420
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:48,948
Si Xian. Ruan Si Xian.

421
00:39:57,585 --> 00:39:59,456
Hello, Auntie.

422
00:40:10,210 --> 00:40:11,999
Just wait a bit!

423
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:13,243
Ruan.

424
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:16,904
What took you so long? Come in.

425
00:40:16,905 --> 00:40:18,819
Help me tidy up.

426
00:40:25,578 --> 00:40:27,411
What's with that face?

427
00:40:27,412 --> 00:40:29,757
Shouldn't you be congratulating me
on my new place?

428
00:40:29,758 --> 00:40:33,581
Congrats on moving from a luxury apartment
to this old dump?

429
00:40:33,582 --> 00:40:36,727
No matter how fancy Mingchen Residences was,
it wasn't mine.

430
00:40:36,728 --> 00:40:38,760
But this place is mine.

431
00:40:40,315 --> 00:40:44,583
I finally bought
back the apartment my dad left me.

432
00:40:44,584 --> 00:40:48,133
I guess I've achieved a little goal of my own.

433
00:40:48,134 --> 00:40:51,357
I get the logic,
but I still can't smile about it.

434
00:40:51,358 --> 00:40:55,283
You worked so hard,
yet this is where you ended up.

435
00:40:55,284 --> 00:40:58,970
That's why I asked you to come
and help me set it up.

436
00:40:58,971 --> 00:41:01,035
I think my place is pretty great.

437
00:41:01,036 --> 00:41:05,821
It may be an old apartment,
but its layout and lighting are good.

438
00:41:05,822 --> 00:41:07,993
And...

439
00:41:07,994 --> 00:41:12,561
ever since I got back,
I've felt especially close to it.

440
00:41:14,058 --> 00:41:18,556
It's like my dad is right here with me.

441
00:41:22,329 --> 00:41:23,953
Your dad?

442
00:41:23,954 --> 00:41:26,406
Is your dad with you?

443
00:41:28,433 --> 00:41:30,439
Hello, mister.

444
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:32,185
You seem like a nice guy.

445
00:41:32,186 --> 00:41:35,370
You wouldn't give me jump scares, right?

446
00:41:35,371 --> 00:41:37,095
Why are you so tense?

447
00:41:37,760 --> 00:41:39,384
I was just making a comparison.

448
00:41:39,385 --> 00:41:42,171
You really got spooked. Get back to work.

449
00:41:43,779 --> 00:41:46,043
I thought you called me over
because something good happened.

450
00:41:46,043 --> 00:41:48,308
So Xuan bosses me around, and you do too.

451
00:41:48,309 --> 00:41:50,759
I'm just your workhorse.

452
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:52,624
That's right. It's good that you know.

453
00:42:15,232 --> 00:42:17,105
Actually,

454
00:42:18,651 --> 00:42:23,441
I've always felt
that Lu Ming is right beside me.

455
00:42:29,378 --> 00:42:33,624
The other night,
I was so scared when you almost got hurt.

456
00:42:33,625 --> 00:42:39,880
I kept telling Lu Ming,
if you can hear me, please keep Ruan safe.

457
00:42:41,087 --> 00:42:44,288
Tell me, do you think he heard me?

458
00:42:49,370 --> 00:42:51,072
Thank you.

459
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:57,963
Am I being ridiculous and stupid?

460
00:42:57,964 --> 00:43:01,229
Clearly,
it's because you have amazing flying skills.

461
00:43:01,230 --> 00:43:06,449
I believe a lot of people must have helped me.

462
00:43:06,450 --> 00:43:08,375
Maybe it was my dad.

463
00:43:09,503 --> 00:43:11,323
Maybe it was Lu Ming.

464
00:43:15,950 --> 00:43:17,929
I plan to move on, too.

465
00:43:19,146 --> 00:43:22,839
People can't live in the past forever.

466
00:43:24,173 --> 00:43:30,137
I need to look ahead for Lu Ming,
to see what the future looks like.

